From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: Scan out AFBC on RK3528's cluster window

RK3528's Cluster0 decodes AFBC through the RK3568 cluster registers the
driver already drives, YUV 4:2:0 included, so a video decoder's AFBC
pictures can be scanned out without being written linear first. Offer
the AFBC modifiers on it.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c
index 216d5e8..184aa4e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_vop2_reg.c
@@ -2738,7 +2738,7 @@ static const struct vop2_win_data rk3528_vop_win_data[] = {
 		.possible_vp_mask = BIT(0),
 		.formats = formats_cluster,
 		.nformats = ARRAY_SIZE(formats_cluster),
-		.format_modifiers = format_modifiers,
+		.format_modifiers = format_modifiers_afbc,
 		.layer_sel_id = { 0, 0xf, 0xf, 0xf },
 		.supported_rotations = DRM_MODE_REFLECT_X | DRM_MODE_REFLECT_Y,
 		.type = DRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY,
@@ -2746,7 +2746,7 @@ static const struct vop2_win_data rk3528_vop_win_data[] = {
 		.axi_uv_r_id = 3,
 		.max_upscale_factor = 4,
 		.max_downscale_factor = 4,
-		.feature = WIN_FEATURE_CLUSTER,
+		.feature = WIN_FEATURE_AFBDC | WIN_FEATURE_CLUSTER,
 	},
 };
 
